+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The directory answers the inverse question as well: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The specialty directory lists every specialty the clinic knows, each by its stored name, together with the veterinarians holding it, and each veterinarian is named first name then last name `[REQ-VET-003]`. It presents specialties rather than the veterinarian roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it, and every specialty fits on the one page. The page is reached by its own address alone: nothing in the system links to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name with the veterinarians holding it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding a specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown under that specialty as first name then last name, as in "Helen Leary".
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the specialty directory is opened, then that specialty is still listed, with no veterinarian shown against it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the specialty directory is opened, then all of them are shown on one page rather than a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the specialty directory's address, when it is requested directly, then the page is served, and no other page of the system carries a link to it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty is shown under each of them.
+2. Specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one, and so are the veterinarians within each specialty.
+3. Specialty and veterinarian names are stored data and are shown as stored. The page's own fixed wording falls under `REQ-LANG-002`, like that of every other page.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
